    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d368">

                <pb facs="0587" n="485" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg485"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.5123/2311: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Atherton</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-02-21T16:00:00+00:00">February 21,
                            1935—4 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 12:22 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>76. Embassy has received various requests, including one from London’s largest
                    retail establishment, inquiring as to truth of press reports published here that
                    United States Treasury is enforcing article 674 of the Income Tax
                        Regulations<anchor n="6" xml:id="d368-f1"/> under which British subjects
                    visiting America for business must pay tax on that portion of their British
                    salaries which accrues while they are in the United States. Business houses
                    point out this raises a serious question in regard to their buyers visiting
                    America and I should appreciate data to enable me to make adequate reply.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Atherton</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d368-f1" n="6" xml:id="d368-f1-content">
                <p>U. S. Treasury Department, Bureau of Internal Revenue, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Regulations 77 Relating to the Income Tax Under the Revenue Act of
                        1982</hi>, p. 214.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
